// Hakuro's light, and his parts grown from others, held against the old code at one pose
// (`old_pose::PALETTE`). The literals are what rywible/wrela at 7ae6711e made of him: the
// combat lab's pixel's normal (`chart::Vertex::normal_from` of the shading form
// content/humanoid/fighter.wrela chose for the part) and its vertex's `place.z` at places of
// his left arm (its elbow folded), his trunk (its fork capped) and his left index finger
// (capped at both ends); and, for his left thumb on his palm, his head on his neck, and his
// coat's left shoulder and left sleeve on its body, each place's vertex from `vertex_onto`
// (where it goes, its normal and its `place.z`) and its pixel's normal. They were written by a
// scratch tool run on the old toolchain, which copies the old vertex programs' bodies (they
// can't run on the CPU there) and calls the old engine for all they use, and are made again with
//
//     cd /Users/ryanwible/projects/wrela-notes/next/scratch/bodies/old
//     ~/.wrela/toolchains/0.33.0/bin/wrela tool tools/forms-light > ../forms/old_light.txt
//
// then old_light_file.py in /Users/ryanwible/projects/wrela-notes/next/scratch/bodies/forms.
// A point, a normal and a share of the light here are held within `WITHIN` of the old ones.

use hakuro::{charted_as, charted_at_rest, jacket_edges}
use old_pose::PALETTE
use shading::{light_at, lit_of, vertex_of}

